# Voice-brain turn-taking  `[capability: voice — desktop only]`

Speaking + listening is a real-time mode — and it exists ONLY on the desktop body. Get the mode wrong and a
headless brain tries to speak into a stub.

**When to use:** you are on the desktop body, in a voice interaction — deciding when to speak vs listen.

## The stack (desktop-only)
- **Kokoro** — text-to-speech (`Autopoet.Kokoro`, local neural voice).
- **Moonshine** — speech-to-text (`Autopoet.Stt.Moonshine`), the STT lane.
- These are DESKTOP features, gated by your **body**, not by a grant: the cloud / headless brain has them
  **stubbed** (`cloud_stubs/`) — voice is simply not available there.

## The discipline
- **Detect your body first** — if voice is stubbed (you're on cloud), degrade to text; never speak into a
  stub. The mode must be legible — you are never wrong about whether you have a voice.
- **Turn-taking** — decide when to speak vs listen; respect barge-in; keep a latency budget (audio timing
  is a real determinism risk).
- **Desktop-gated** — on any headless / cloud body this skill is inert, and that's correct: degrade, don't
  fake it.
